--- This file defines the persistent object class.  Other storage files import it,
--- so it stays loaded even when the persistent object APIs are left out.

--- This module defines PersistObj class that models the persistent object of the G.P. documentation.

--- @kind state
--- @feature persistent
omod PERSISTENT-OBJECT is
  pr OBJECT-ID .
  pr TRUSTED-STORAGE-OBJECT .
  pr FILE-ID .
  pr STORAGE-IDENTIFER .
  pr LIST{Data} .
  pr SET{DataAccessFlag} .

--- The open handles of a persistent object: oh(H, FLAGS) for each object handle H on it, opened with
--- the data access flags FLAGS.  The sharing rules of TEE_OpenPersistentObject compare the flags of a
--- new handle with all of them.  A rule sees only part of the configuration, so the handles are listed
--- on the object instead of being searched for in the configuration.
  sort OpenHandles .
  op noHandles : -> OpenHandles [ctor] .
  op oh : Oid Set{DataAccessFlag} -> OpenHandles [ctor] .
  op __ : OpenHandles OpenHandles -> OpenHandles [ctor assoc comm id: noHandles] .

--- The persistent object class.  The data stream is embedded in the object as a list of data fragments.
  class PersistObj | file-name : FileName , data-stream : List{Data} , open-handles : OpenHandles .
  subclass PersistObj < CryptoObj .

endom
